{"chunk_id": "76192ae68794", "text": "Kichaka, consumed by lust for Sairindhri (Draupadi in disguise), begs his sister Queen Sudeshna to help him obtain her. Despite knowing Kichaka\u2019s character and Draupadi\u2019s fears, Sudeshna deceitfully sends Draupadi to Kichaka\u2019s house under the pretext of fetching wine. Terrified yet steadfast in her fidelity to her husbands, Draupadi prays for protection; the sun\u2011god Surya secretly assigns a Rakshasa to guard her. Kichaka attempts to seduce and then assault her, but she resists fiercely and escapes to the royal court. There, in front of the king, Kichaka drags and kicks her. The invisible guardian strikes him down, while Bhima burns with rage but is restrained by Yudhishthira to preserve their disguise. The episode intensifies the moral outrage and foreshadows Kichaka\u2019s impending doom.\nKichaka schemes to lure Sairindhri; Draupadi is assaulted but protected by a divine Rakshasa while Bhima burns with rage yet restrains himself to preserve their disguise.\nThemes: lust and abuse of power, divine protection, restraint under disguise, honor and chastity, rising vengeance", "vector": [0.016520099714398384, -0.011390102095901966, 0.01799951307475567, -0.006116272881627083, -0.004061534069478512, 0.032684046775102615, -0.019355639815330505, -0.018780313432216644, 0.005174517631530762, -0.02678009681403637, 0.01453385315835476, -0.0027944447938352823, 0.028903327882289886, 0.004999864846467972, -0.006924469955265522, 0.015917377546429634, 0.04876580461859703, -0.007445003837347031, 0.029697826132178307, -0.030656704679131508, -0.016451610252261162, 0.0035581227857619524, 0.0027516377158463, 0.027588294818997383, -0.04920414835214615, 0.0176844522356987, 0.007924443110823631, -0.029122499749064445, -0.004006740637123585, -0.006619683932512999, -0.019163865596055984, -0.01065724529325962, 0.009527139365673065, -0.013814694248139858, -0.03712228313088417, -0.010376431047916412, -0.01806800439953804, -0.030410135164